 **Rationale**: Multiple releases shipped with wrong version numbers, no release notes, or
 untested regressions. The checklist exists because each of these has happened.
 
+### Issue Closure
+
+A fix ships with a comment on the issue saying what changed. It MUST NOT ship with the issue
+closed. Closing is the reporter's move: they filed it, so they are the one who can say the
+thing they hit stopped happening. If nobody answers within a week of the release carrying the
+fix, close it then.
+
+This is the default for every agent working in this repo — comment, never close, unless Tom
+says otherwise in so many words.
+
+**Rationale**: A maintainer closing their own fix asserts the report is resolved without the
+one piece of evidence that would prove it. It also ends the thread: a reporter coming back to
+say "still broken on 2026.2" is now replying to something already marked done.
+
 ### Commit Discipline
 
 - Never commit `iris.key` or any license file. (A prior incident required git history rewriting.)
